# Always revalidate the app shell + service worker so a new deploy shows on the
# next load instead of lingering in the browser/CDN cache (prevents stale "whiteout"
# copies). Static assets (icons, images, SEO pages) keep their default caching.

# Clickjacking + MIME + referrer hardening on EVERY page: the app shells are Pages-served, so the
# worker's own security headers don't reach them. frame-ancestors 'none' is a REAL header here (it is
# ignored inside a <meta> CSP), which closes the clickjacking gap the audit flagged (AUTH-P2).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/atlas.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/admin.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/atlas-sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/atlas-manifest.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
